today the council adapted without debate  regulation on energy efficiency labeling  which allows customers to be more aware  of the energy efficiency and energy  consumption of household appliances thus  helping them to reduce their energy  costs and contributing to the moderation  of energy demand the council also  reached a general approach Cannella on a  proposal for a revised directive on  energy performance of buildings its aim  is to be to promote energy efficiency in  buildings and to support cost-effective  building renovation with a view to  long-term goal of decarbonizing the  highly inefficient existing European  building stock we are very proud of  securing these council positions we send  a signal to the public that the council  is taking its energy and climate calls  commitment seriously and is ready to  engage in negotiations with the European  Parliament as soon as possible the  council was informed by the Commission  on recent developments in the field of  external energy relations including on  the recent Commission requests for a  negotiation mandate on an agreement  between EU and the Russian Federation on  the north stream to pipeline the  Commission explained that the aim of the  agreement is avoid legal uncertainty and  then sure that the onshore part of the  pipeline complies with all use relevant  legislation in this field such as the  internal in general market security of  gas supply competition and the  environment arose the 30 percent energy  efficiency target agreed today will  increase Europe's GDP of 70 billion  euros will create about 400,000 new jobs  especially amongst SMEs and will reduce  our - imports by 12% by 2070
 

